# Commits that only ran a formatter over the code. git blame looks past
# them with `git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs`, and
# GitHub's blame does by itself.
#
# The `# format-...:` lines above an id say how that commit was made, for
# carrying work made before it across it (runner/src/format-replay.ts; tb land
# does it by itself, scripts/replay-over-format.sh by hand, and a fork
# bringing in Mike's release with --merge):
#   format-subject  the commit's subject, which finds it until its id is
#                   written below it (tb land and sync-main.sh can both
#                   rebase it on the way to GitHub, so the id is filled in
#                   from origin/main afterwards)
#   format-command  what made it, run from the top of a copy of the tree
#   format-tool     instead of format-command: a tool that may also add and
#                   delete files under its paths (a copy older than this key
#                   skips the entry, so it stops at the conflict rather than
#                   lose the files the tool made)
#   format-paths    the folders (or files) it formats (and only reads from)
#   format-config   files taken from the format commit itself while
#                   formatting an older tree, so it's formatted the same way
# The tree's own config files are put back afterwards. A format commit
# that's reverted comes out of this list in the same commit.

